/* op_descriptors.def — THE canonical list of every op_descriptor.
 *
 * One OP_DESC(symbol) entry per descriptor, ordered by id.  This single list
 * feeds BOTH the extern declarations (op_descriptors.h) and the registry array
 * (op_descriptor.c) via the X-macro idiom, so the two can never drift.  The
 * descriptor DEFINITIONS still live next to their hooks in the owning modules.
 *
 * To add an operation:
 *
 *  1. define the descriptor next to its hooks in the owning .c;
 *  2. add one OP_DESC line here, ordered by id;
 *  3. write serialize/deserialize so the op can be replayed by the edit
 *     history — or add its id to opaque_by_design[] in
 *     src/tests/test_op_descriptor.c with the reason it cannot be.  There is
 *     no third option: a descriptor that is neither fails that test, which is
 *     deliberate.  Without a serializer the op is recorded as an opaque
 *     barrier and the user cannot edit any step before it;
 *  4. add replay_pre only if the hook reads something outside its params
 *     struct.  For an external file operand, pin it by path + size + SHA-256;
 *  5. add a round-trip test to src/tests/test_nde_serializers.c;
 *  6. if the hook can compute a sub-rectangle of the image, set
 *     OP_ROI_CAPABLE so region previews can use it;
 *  7. and then write roi_halo() — how much INPUT context it needs around that
 *     rectangle.  This is a separate question from (6): 0 is the right answer
 *     for a pixel-local op and does not mean "no region support";
 *  8. and set roi_halo_exact, and add the op to src/tests/roi_halo_test.c.
 *     TRUE means the test asserts the halo is a true bound on the op's
 *     spatial support; FALSE means it only reports (iterative and non-local
 *     ops have no such bound);
 *  9. optionally register a native amend editor in gui-gtk4/nde_editors.c.
 *     If it has a live preview, call roi_declare_op() at dialog startup and
 *     pass the descriptor to nde_amend_note_update().
 *
 * Steps 3 and 6-8 are the ones most often forgotten, which is why each has a
 * test that fails when it is.  See doc/NDE.rst and doc/WritingFeature.rst in
 * siril-contrib-doc for the long form.
 */
